1
00:00:02,978 --> 00:00:04,759
Ah! Miss Stewart! Welcome!

2
00:00:04,759 --> 00:00:05,624
How are you?

3
00:00:05,624 --> 00:00:07,100
Fine, Somsak. And you?

4
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:08,443
Fine, thank you.

5
00:00:08,443 --> 00:00:10,550
This is my friend Harry Bennett.

6
00:00:10,550 --> 00:00:11,446
Pleased to meet you.

7
00:00:11,446 --> 00:00:12,779
Very nice to meet you.

8
00:00:12,779 --> 00:00:15,761
Any friend of Miss Stewart's is welcome at Somsak's.

9
00:00:15,761 --> 00:00:18,224
Follow me, please.

10
00:00:18,224 --> 00:00:19,211
I like it here.

11
00:00:19,211 --> 00:00:23,384
I do, too. I come here often.

12
00:00:23,384 --> 00:00:26,122
A special place for special people.

13
00:00:26,122 --> 00:00:29,938
Thank you, Somsak.

14
00:00:29,938 --> 00:00:36,391
Well! Nice restaurant.

15
00:00:36,391 --> 00:00:37,683
Would you like something to drink?

16
00:00:37,683 --> 00:00:40,421
Yes, I'd like a glass of ginger ale with ice.

17
00:00:40,421 --> 00:00:42,874
Harry, what would you like?

18
00:00:42,874 --> 00:00:44,787
Do you have a dry white wine?

19
00:00:44,787 --> 00:00:46,334
How about a California chablis?

20
00:00:46,334 --> 00:00:48,288
Chablis is fine.

21
00:00:48,288 --> 00:00:50,466
What would you like to eat?

22
00:00:50,466 --> 00:00:52,492
I'd like the mee krob.

23
00:00:52,492 --> 00:00:54,405
Harry, would you like to see a menu?

24
00:00:54,405 --> 00:00:55,372
No, it's Ok.

25
00:00:55,372 --> 00:01:01,010
I'll have the mee krob also.

26
00:01:01,010 --> 00:01:03,433
What is it?

27
00:01:03,433 --> 00:01:06,954
Crispy fried noodles. I love them.

28
00:01:06,954 --> 00:01:08,236
May I bring you a salad?

29
00:01:08,236 --> 00:01:09,397
Oh yes.

30
00:01:09,397 --> 00:01:10,872
What do you recommend today?

31
00:01:10,872 --> 00:01:12,969
I recommend rose-petal salad.

32
00:01:12,969 --> 00:01:15,961
Special for new friends.

33
00:01:15,961 --> 00:01:17,854
Rose-petal salad?

34
00:01:17,854 --> 00:01:19,584
Why not?

35
00:01:19,584 --> 00:01:24,846
I'll take care of everything.

36
00:01:24,846 --> 00:01:27,696
I hope you're hungry.

37
00:01:27,696 --> 00:01:35,400
What? Oh, yes. Starving. Well, I...

38
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:39,431
Well, I ...

39
00:01:39,431 --> 00:01:41,863
What do you do at Universe Toy Company?

40
00:01:41,863 --> 00:01:44,845
I'm the vice-president of new toy development.

41
00:01:44,845 --> 00:01:46,789
Terrific!

42
00:01:46,789 --> 00:01:49,374
I know you 're a CPA.

43
00:01:49,374 --> 00:01:51,236
That's true. Harry Bennett,

44
00:01:51,236 --> 00:01:53,211
certified public accountant.

45
00:01:53,211 --> 00:01:54,972
I love numbers.

46
00:01:54,972 --> 00:01:56,050
I do some work for Smith and Dale,

47
00:01:56,050 --> 00:01:58,086
Your company's accounting firm.

48
00:01:58,086 --> 00:02:01,506
And so...

49
00:02:01,506 --> 00:02:03,073
Here we are.

50
00:02:03,073 --> 00:02:04,671
Yes.

51
00:02:04,671 --> 00:02:05,862
I have a daughter.

52
00:02:05,862 --> 00:02:08,213
I know. How old is she?

53
00:02:08,213 --> 00:02:09,688
She's nine years old.

54
00:02:09,688 --> 00:02:11,785
That's a nice age. What's her name?

55
00:02:11,785 --> 00:02:13,291
Michelle.

56
00:02:13,291 --> 00:02:25,952
Do you have a picture of her?

57
00:02:25,952 --> 00:02:28,364
She's very pretty.

58
00:02:28,364 --> 00:02:36,089
Thank you.

59
00:02:36,089 --> 00:02:38,806
Rose-petal salad.

60
00:02:38,806 --> 00:02:42,318
And there's a phone call for you, Mr. Bennett.

61
00:02:42,318 --> 00:02:45,177
Excuse me, Susan.

62
00:02:45,177 --> 00:02:47,762
I hope nothing is wrong.

63
00:02:47,762 --> 00:02:49,096
I'll get the rest of the dinner.

64
00:02:49,096 --> 00:03:03,517
Excuse me.

65
00:03:03,517 --> 00:03:05,482
Please forgive me, Susan, but...

66
00:03:05,482 --> 00:03:09,858
I have to leave. I feel terrible, but...

67
00:03:09,858 --> 00:03:11,619
What's the matter?

68
00:03:11,619 --> 00:03:13,512
My daughter isn't feeling well.

69
00:03:13,512 --> 00:03:16,066
Oh no! Is it serious?

70
00:03:16,066 --> 00:03:19,985
I don't know. The baby-sitter says she has a stomachache,

71
00:03:19,985 --> 00:03:20,850
and she's crying.

72
00:03:20,850 --> 00:03:22,600
I'll have to go home.

73
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:23,547
Will you forgive me?

74
00:03:23,547 --> 00:03:26,641
Of course. I'm so sorry for Michelle.

75
00:03:26,641 --> 00:03:28,473
And you didn't have a chance to eat.

76
00:03:28,473 --> 00:03:29,959
Oh, it's OK.

77
00:03:29,959 --> 00:03:31,200
Let me take you home first.

78
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:33,785
No, no. Please, go ahead.

79
00:03:33,785 --> 00:03:35,831
It's our first date.

80
00:03:35,831 --> 00:03:37,398
We'll make another.

81
00:03:37,398 --> 00:03:40,370
Please don't worry.

82
00:03:40,370 --> 00:03:41,307
I'll phone you.

83
00:03:41,307 --> 00:03:45,347
I hope your daughter is all right. Good-bye.

84
00:03:45,347 --> 00:03:45,347
Good-bye.
